       "title": "The gaseous state",
       "page": 162,
       "src": "notes",
       "enriched": true,
       "body": [
        "A gas is described by pressure P, volume V, temperature T and amount n.",
        "T(K) = t(C) + 273. Never use Celsius in Charles or PV = nRT."
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "title": "Gas behaviour",
       "page": 1,
       "body": [
        "P, V, T, n linked by gas laws. Boyle: PV=const (T fixed). Charles: V/T=const (P fixed).",
        "Ideal gas: PV=nRT (use consistent units)."
       ],
       "id": "chem11-u5-deep1"
      },
      {
       "type": "text",
       "title": "Combined gas law",
       "body": [
        "P₁V₁/T₁ = P₂V₂/T₂ when n fixed.",
        "Always use Kelvin for T."
       ],
       "id": "chem11-u5-xtra1",
